{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061160-2e-spellcasting-dramatic-failures-and-paradox","id":1061160,"title":"[2E] Spellcasting - Dramatic Failures and Paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-11T01:11:02-08:00","id":1061160,"title":"[2E] Spellcasting - Dramatic Failures and Paradox","content":"Our lovely <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> made some interesting point on game mechanics:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061153#post1061153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currenlty airing anime Little Witch Academia shows a lot how Dramatic Failures on Spellcasting and Paradox can make Mage game fun while also progressing character arcs and not necessarily just act as story derailing punishments. Do Paradox in that way and players will be tempted to Dramatic Failure that Failure and will be more willing to not do everything they can to overpower Paradoxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I getting this right, or does Dramatic Failures on spellcasting rolls means that character get's Paradox on this spell? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If not, how the system hack like that impact the game setting then? I was thinking sometime about running this way, but I'm not sure what is official rules stand on the matter and how would this change game world.<br /> <br /> P.S. How good is <i>Little Witch Academia</i> as anime? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T01:20:50-08:00","id":1061163,"title":"","content":"Little Witch Academia is very fun. It has the spark of imagination and love that makes difference between Hogwarts and Generic Magic School Number Sixty Three. Episode Eight even contains a straight on Astral Journey.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failures of Spellcasting Rolls don't produce Paradox in core rules. Instead, you suffer from a Condition that has to be somewhat related to the spell you tried to cast. Hello beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-11-2017, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T02:57:57-08:00","id":1061180,"title":"","content":"Yea, Dramatic Failures on Spellcasting don't cause Paradox. Paradox is checked before the spell is cast and if released can impose penalties to the Spellcasting dicepool. Would be a bit of a dick move to have it cause enough penalties as to make a failure dramatic and then have that failure cause another Paradox on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T03:26:15-08:00","id":1061185,"title":"","content":"Well, I throw out Paradox dice penalty out od window in the first place, so this particular side of rules is no problem for me. And I do this as I think making 'Paradox is DIRECTLY bad to yours magic' makes it Paradox obviously bad option for rach character casting- when in my take even 'good' PCs can 'wet the toe' with Abyss if they see strategic advantage in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}